& [Constructive]
  + a deterministic operation DAG is the missing semantic bridge between complete closure declaration and later physical executor commission
  + reusing exact P0 forms avoids a parallel manifest language and preserves material source target receipt and denial identities
  + formula-bound phases make the plan inspectable and allow user-facing audit before effects

& [Critical]
  + operation names can motivate action and therefore must visibly retain proposed unresolved ungranted and zero-effect state
  + embedding upstream bytes risks accepting recomposed or stale P0 data unless strict P0 parse and digest replay occur before planning
  + synthetic fixture evidence can be laundered into a real deployment claim unless input class and known fixture identity agree
  + rollback preparation and receipt candidate language can overclaim recovery or installation unless all observation and state fields are false or zero

& [Synthesis]
  + close every operation kind phase count dependency and capability requirement, conserve all P0 denials, use no effect API and independently replay raw retained bytes plus fully redigested semantic adversaries
